From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 01:02:42 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 080/207] runner: poll a held stream's run each millisecond;
 host cost bench on real replies

A stream held at a runner trigger is settled by a translation or a run on another thread, which never wakes the engine
loop, so the hold waited for the idle loop's full sleep (20 ms with a round planner, 100 ms without) once to start the
run and once to collect it. While a stream is held the idle wait is 1 ms. Replies are unchanged; only the hold is
shorter. bench-runner-cost replays real replies through a reply session: ns per token off, scanning, firing.
